<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-27T23:01:37.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-html-tags-13098f8b-eb31-4092-88aa-49d6672215f0",
        "text": "Imagine a webpage like a beautiful house! What kind of house would you build?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/1260ce423273225f5d7e660e78ef17d4-test-lesson-intro-html-tags-panel-1-a7964312-8d80-433c-b136-d96317a7963c.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-html-tags-03b801c0-c0e9-448f-aeaa-4832818454f5",
        "text": "HTML is like the 'bones' or the *frame* of that house. It gives the webpage its shape and tells it where everything goes.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/c6c5c917b3e8de331ab1f45caad58b68-test-lesson-intro-html-tags-panel-2-34cc0671-45ec-4fdb-a1e5-f2b311de046b.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-html-tags-ca10d8db-db38-463a-bbc1-a1c62f25bd06",
        "text": "Just like a house has a main roof or a big front door, web pages have important titles! We use the `<h1>` tag to create big, important headings.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/585bac9cc2a23496910eb333774b0521-test-lesson-intro-html-tags-panel-3-c905bd84-665d-43a3-b12b-8ba8e52853b8.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-html-tags-8636fc12-8697-4ef1-a24a-24f5d3da886b",
        "text": "And just like rooms have walls for pictures or furniture, web pages have paragraphs of text. The `<p>` tag helps us make regular paragraphs of text for our stories or descriptions.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/399bb1317ed976ae4f4c7cee1b3434f3-test-lesson-intro-html-tags-panel-4-60e8973c-f1f9-45fd-a2e5-db001322e244.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Introduce students to what a webpage is and explain that HTML is like the 'bones' or 'structure' of a webpage. Use simple analogies suitable for K-5 students. Show visual examples of how tags look and their basic purpose in defining content like titles and paragraphs."
  },
  "published": true,
